    {
      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>A solar PV commissioning record must stand up to an MCS audit, a DNO query, an insurer and a homeowner years later. It ties string tests, inverter settings and earthing into a handover pack. The best tool gets it written while you are still on the roof with the meter in hand.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>A UK solar PV install is a notifiable electrical job under BS 7671 and Part P. It is an MCS install if it claims the Microgeneration Certification Scheme.</li><li>The DNO must be told. G98 is for small single-premises systems. G99 is where G98 limits are passed.</li><li>Commissioning records string voltage and current, insulation resistance, earthing, inverter settings and AC checks, with photos.</li><li>The handover pack joins it all to the MCS certificate, electrical certificate and DNO papers.</li><li>Software records the data. It does not replace MCS certification or a competent installer.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The point",
      "heading": "What PV commissioning software is for",
      "html": "<p>A grid-connected solar PV install is an electrical installation. It falls under BS 7671. The DC and AC work is notifiable under Part P in England and Wales. An MCS install must also meet the MCS standards and the IET Code of Practice for Grid-Connected Solar PV.</p><p>Software makes none of that valid. The MCS-certified installer does, with calibrated instruments. Software makes the record easy to finish on site and quick to turn into a handover pack.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Grid connection",
      "heading": "G98, G99 and the DNO notification",
      "html": "<p>The Distribution Network Operator must be told, before or soon after energising. Small single-premises systems within limits generally use G98. Larger systems fall under G99, with an application before connection. The rules change, so check the current ones.</p><p>Quickler can record reference numbers, inverter details and photos of the isolation and metering. It is not the DNO portal. It does not send the notification. This is general information.</p>"
    },
