      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What is a solar PV commissioning report?</h3><p>The record made when a PV system is energised and tested. Per-string voltage and current, DC insulation resistance, earthing and polarity, inverter settings, AC checks, and photos of the array, isolators and labels. It joins the MCS certificate, electrical certificate and DNO notification in the handover pack.</p><h3>Does a solar PV install have to follow MCS?</h3><p>MCS is not compulsory for every install. It is needed if the system is to be certified under the Microgeneration Certification Scheme, which most homeowners and scheme routes expect. An MCS install must meet the MCS standards and the IET Code of Practice.</p><h3>Do I need to notify the DNO for a solar PV system?</h3><p>Yes. Small single-premises systems within limits generally use G98. Larger systems use G99, with an application before connection. Check the current thresholds and your DNO's process. Quickler does not send the notification.</p><h3>Can I capture PV commissioning over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Answer by text, voice note or photo. The report writes itself. No new app and no login.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/ev-charger-installation-report-uk.html\">EV charger installation report</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/heat-pump-commissioning-checklist-uk.html\">Heat pump commissioning checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/battery-storage-inspection-report-uk.html\">Battery storage inspection report</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/eicr-software-uk.html\">EICR and electrical reporting software</a></li></ul>"
